<?php

namespace Laravel\Ai;

use Laravel\Ai\Files\Audio;
use Laravel\Ai\Files\Document;
use Laravel\Ai\Files\Image;
use Laravel\Ai\Files\Video;
use Laravel\Ai\PendingResponses\PendingEmbeddingsGeneration;

class Embeddings
{
    /**
     * The write-side of indirect prompt injection via RAG: anything embedded
     * here can be retrieved into a future prompt verbatim. PoisonedRAG (Zou
     * et al., USENIX Security 2025) shows 5 poisoned docs → 90% targeted
     * attack success. Mark the inputs as an llm_prompt sink so that
     * user-controlled text reaching this method surfaces a finding.
     *
     * The same method also embeds the query side of a search, where nothing is
     * stored and no generative prompt runs; that call is a low-signal hit. It is
     * one method for both jobs upstream, and the `llm_prompt` kind ships
     * advisory (see `findPromptInjection` in docs/config.md), so the write-side
     * coverage is kept rather than traded away.
     *
     * The union is copied from vendor/laravel/ai/src/Embeddings.php. Narrowing
     * it to `string[]` here made a valid `Document::fromString()` argument a
     * false `InvalidArgument`, and native types match on both sides (`array`),
     * so bin/ci/check-laravel-ai-stub-parity.php cannot see docblock drift of
     * this shape.
     *
     * @param  array<int, string|Audio|Document|Image|Video>  $inputs
     *
     * @psalm-taint-sink llm_prompt $inputs
     */
    public static function for(array $inputs): PendingEmbeddingsGeneration {}
}
